      "sourceRowFinding": "Literal content clause is authentic, but courseLevel=unspecified discards the actual right-hand LK-additional column on PDF30. PDF33 independently specifies LK mechanism representation with structural formulas.",
      "carrierDecision": "accepted for c3077d95-f3fe-5579-8493-cb92992809c4 at LK only",
      "narrowerObligations": "Alcohol monomer formation FROM halogenalkane, nucleophilic substitution MECHANISM, polyester context; structural formulas and electron-pair arrows in the precise carrier retain this. Generic donor/acceptor recognition or a net equation alone is less than the LK mechanism.",
      "broaderUnion": "9b942490 includes actual whole polyester/polyamide condensation, chain ends and finite-chain stoichiometry. c2d3f72b expands to general SN explanation, equations and halide-ion detection via 3899edf4,d4928773,41396457. Halide proof and polyamide/whole-polycondensation scope are not obligations of this particular alcohol-monomer clause. All current edges are partial; that qualification is legitimate and must not become a full-union official-credit claim.",
      "specificDelta": "Restore the original LK course qualifier in source authority; restrict full-clause source credit to the mechanism/monomer carrier. Keep any useful broader SkillPilot targets with their separate authority; do not remove GK polycondensation merely because this clause is LK.",
      "projectionObservation": "The current BB LK view directly targets c3077d95; BB GK does not. Both directly target 9b942490. This avoids claiming a demonstrated runtime LK-to-GK leak; extraction course fidelity still needs revision.",
