      "decision": "revise",
      "sourceRowFinding": "The actual Leistungsfach clause is one further SELECTED substance group and requires a connected scientific-historical, current and future-oriented R&D explanation. Farbstoffe/Waschmittel/Pharmazeutika/Komplexverbindungen/Silikone are examples of alternatives, not a compulsory list of five complete disciplines.",
      "carrierDecision": "accepted for d815960a-21ab-5a42-8b23-ecd20d03db19 as the selected dye-group route",
      "narrowerObligations": "All three time perspectives and the application-oriented research/development link must remain connected; merely knowing a group, its synthesis or uses is insufficient. The dye carrier and BW-B1/BW-B2 contract preserve that link.",
      "broaderUnion": "a78aacf9 detergent component functions, f71a2c0a painkiller composition/use/consumption, e56040b5 plus silicone formation/nanosurface descendants, and fa21e8e1 plus all dye optics/mechanisms/fibre/vat/health/history descendants are substantially broader than this selected-group clause. Nano applications also belong to neighbouring 3.4.8 clauses; a whole dye cluster is not made compulsory by the example word Farbstoffe.",
      "specificDelta": "Retain the source literal, LK and one-selected-group condition. Bind full competence to the explicit dye research route; label the other edges as partial topical support or separately sourced broader SkillPilot targets, not satisfaction of all three perspectives or an official duty to study every family. Current broad target policy can include all authored topics without changing the official choice.",
      "materialObservation": "The supplied actual BASF Indigo history case is useful partial historical-economic context: chronology investment is not profit and an interested corporate source is not independent confirmation. That case alone cannot replace the current/future R&D obligations. No missing Komplex group is asserted because the source expressly permits selecting one group.",
      "primaryPages": [
        42
      ]
    },
